-- title:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data, segment 12, group 033, part 2 (heights ≈718382.0222–≈718519.1766)
-- statement:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data for the zeros of $\zeta(1/2+it)$ with $t\in[≈718382.0222,\,≈718519.1766]$: part 2 of group 033 of segment 12 of the extension from height $100000$ to $10^6$.
--
--   Each band is a list of records of the structure `RS5.Sample` from the published framework: a dyadic height $t=tn/2^{16}$, a margin $E$ and integer hint fields for the Riemann–Siegel main sum. Consecutive bands share their endpoint sample.
--
--   The data were produced by a program and are not trusted; the kernel checks them in the problems named below. The problem `RH1E6S12.part_033_2` states that every band of the part passes the kernel-evaluated sharp band checker of the framework, which certifies a sign change of Hardy's $Z(t)$ between consecutive samples of opposite sign.
-- source:
--   Computational certificate extending the kernel-checked verification of the Riemann hypothesis on prove2.me (published ArdaRH65K framework, Proved to height 65000; extended to height 100000 by the RHX100000 problems) to height 1000000; data produced by an exact integer Rust port of the framework checkers and checked by the Lean kernel.

